.TH EMAIL\-CLI\-RO 1 "" "email-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
email\-cli\-ro \- read\-only terminal email client for scripts and AI agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B email\-cli\-ro
.RI [ account ]
.RI [ --batch ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B email\-cli\-ro
reads mail over IMAP or the Gmail API and prints it to standard output.
It is the read\-only member of the email\-cli suite: it can only issue
.B FETCH
(with
.BR BODY.PEEK )
and
.B SEARCH
commands, so it never sends, moves, deletes, or changes a flag \- not even
.BR \eSeen .
This makes it safe to hand to automation that must not modify a mailbox.
.PP
For write operations use
.BR email\-cli (1);
for an interactive terminal UI use
.BR email\-tui (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List messages. Unread only by default; see
.B \-\-all
and the virtual folders below.
.TP
.BI show " uid " [ \-\-raw ]
Print one message: headers, then the body as rendered text. HTML mail is
converted to text; attachments are listed, not dumped. With
.B \-\-raw
the stored message is written verbatim instead \- see OPTIONS.
.TP
.B list\-folders
List IMAP folders, with message and unread counts.
.TP
.B list\-labels
List Gmail labels with their IDs.
.TP
.BI list\-attachments " uid"
List the attachments of a message.
.TP
.BI save\-attachment " uid filename " [ dir ]
Write one attachment to disk.
.TP
.B list\-accounts
List configured accounts.
.TP
.BI help " [command]"
Show help for a command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-batch
Disable the interactive pager and use a fixed page size of 100. This is
implied whenever standard output is not a terminal, so a pipe or a captured
subprocess already behaves this way; pass it explicitly when in doubt.
.TP
.B \-\-all
List every message, not just unread ones.
.TP
.BI \-\-folder " name"
Folder to operate on, overriding the configured one. Accepts the virtual
folders described below.
.TP
.BI \-\-label " id-or-name"
Gmail alias for
.BR \-\-folder .
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " n"
At most
.I n
messages (default 100 in batch mode).
.TP
.BI \-\-offset " n"
Start at the
.IR n th
message, 1\-based.
.TP
.BI \-\-from " text"
.RB ( list )
Keep only messages whose From field contains
.I text
(case\-insensitive substring).
.TP
.BI \-\-since " YYYY-MM-DD"
.RB ( list )
Keep only messages dated on or after this day, inclusive.
.TP
.BI \-\-before " YYYY-MM-DD"
.RB ( list )
Keep only messages dated strictly before this day.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-accounts
.RB ( list )
Repeat the listing for every configured account, each under an
.RI "\(dq=== " account " ===\(dq"
heading. Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-json ,
since several JSON documents in sequence would not form one parseable value.
.TP
.B \-\-json
.RB ( list )
Emit JSON instead of the table: one object per message, with
.BR uid ", " date ", " from ", " subject ", " folder ", " status ", " flags ", "
.BR unread ", " flagged " and " attachments .
Standard output stays a single parseable document \- the count line and the
paging hint are suppressed, notices go to standard error, and an empty result
is an empty array. Unlike the table, fields are never truncated.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
.RB ( show )
Write the RFC 2822 source exactly as stored: no MIME parsing, no
transfer\-encoding or charset decoding, no HTML rendering, no header
reformatting. Use it to see what the sender actually transmitted \- for
instance the real
.B Content\-Type
line when text looks mis\-decoded.
.TP
.BI \-\-account " email"
Select the account. Required when several are configured; it can also be
given as the first positional argument.
.SH VIRTUAL FOLDERS
.B \-\-folder
also accepts names that are not real folders. They are resolved from the
local store, span every cached folder, and need no server connection.
A message cached in several folders is listed once.
.TP
.B __unread__
Unread messages.
.TP
.B __flagged__
Starred / flagged messages.
.TP
.B __answered__
Messages that were replied to.
.TP
.B __forwarded__
Messages that were forwarded.
.TP
.B __junk__
Messages marked as junk or spam.
.TP
.B __phishing__
Messages flagged as phishing.
.TP
.B __all__
Every cached message, whatever its flags \- the cross\-folder counterpart of a
plain folder listing.
.SH SEARCH
.PP
.B \-\-folder \(dq__search__:<scope>:<query>\(dq
.PP
.I scope
selects the field:
.BR 0 " = Subject, " 1 " = From, " 2 " = To, " 3 " = Body."
The query is a case\-insensitive substring, not a glob. Quote the whole
argument \- it contains colons.
.PP
The search runs against the local store, so it works offline and sees only
messages already cached. Run
.BR email\-sync (1)
first if the mailbox may have unfetched mail.
.PP
Scope
.B 3
searches the
.I decoded
body:
.B base64
and
.B quoted\-printable
parts are decoded, non\-UTF\-8 charsets are converted, and
.B text/html
parts are searched as rendered text. Prefer it over a subject search for
machine\-generated mail \- order confirmations, invoices and receipts
usually carry a generic subject, and the identifying detail (a product
name, an order number) appears only in the body.
.PP
.B \-\-all
has no effect on a search: every cached message is considered.
.SH OUTPUT
Batch output is a fixed\-width table: UID, date, a six\-character status
column, subject, and sender. The subject is truncated to the column width,
so parse the UID and re\-read the full text with
.B show
rather than scraping the table. Status characters, in order:
.PP
.RS
.nf
1  P=phishing  J=junk  N=unread  \-
2  *=starred  \-
3  D=done  \-
4  A=has attachment  \-
5  R=replied  F=forwarded  \-
6  v=DMARC pass  x=DMARC fail  \-
.fi
.RE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
If a text body declares a charset that
.BR iconv (3)
does not know, or the conversion hits an invalid byte sequence, the body is
printed
.I undecoded
\- it cannot be recovered. Since that is otherwise indistinguishable from
correct output, a warning naming the UID and the declared charset is written to
standard error; the message itself still goes to standard output. Use
.B show \-\-raw
to inspect the original headers in that case.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/email\-cli/accounts/<email>/config.ini
Per\-account configuration, mode 0600. IMAP host, user, password and folder;
Gmail accounts store an OAuth2 refresh token instead of a password.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/email\-cli/accounts/<email>/
Local store: cached messages, per\-folder manifests, label indexes and
queued operations. Directory mode 0700.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/email\-cli/logs/session.log
Diagnostics. May contain server responses.
.PP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME " and " XDG_CACHE_HOME
override these locations and take precedence over
.BR HOME .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, non\-zero on failure. Errors go to standard error, results to
standard output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Unread mail across all folders:
.PP
.RS
.nf
email\-cli\-ro \-\-batch list \-\-folder __unread__ \-\-limit 20
.fi
.RE
.PP
Everything from one sender in a date range, as JSON:
.PP
.RS
.nf
email\-cli\-ro \-\-batch list \-\-all \-\-folder __all__ \\
    \-\-from @shop.example \-\-since 2024\-01\-01 \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Find an order confirmation by product name, then read it in full:
.PP
.RS
.nf
email\-cli\-ro \-\-batch list \-\-folder \(dq__search__:3:water heater\(dq
email\-cli\-ro \-\-batch show 0000000000012345 \-\-folder INBOX
.fi
.RE
.PP
A specific sender, when several accounts are configured:
.PP
.RS
.nf
email\-cli\-ro user@example.com \-\-batch list \-\-folder \(dq__search__:1:@shop.example\(dq
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR email\-cli (1),
.BR email\-tui (1),
.BR email\-sync (1),
.BR email\-import\-rules (1)
